Z||000000||lennyb4||04-12-2000||01:44 PM||||Heres one for you general body guys. My car was hit in the rear about two months ago (yea i know driving it in winter....i should be shot). I have the new rear facia, my problem is above the tail light it was damaged also. Its pretty bad, all there but bad. Would it be better to just repair the area w/fiberglass or to try to cut and fit a new section on? And if so what or how would i join the two pieces?||||reg||11
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-12-2000||05:58 PM||||Isn't the rear deck the part above the tail lights?  It may be easy to just replace the whole deck than to repair it.  Now if the part is the rear clip that is broken, thats another story.  It hard to estimate without seeing it.||||reg||5
Z||000002||lennyb4||04-13-2000||08:17 AM||||No its not the rear deck lid. Its the rear upper clip right next to the tail light (pass. side).||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||04-13-2000||11:22 AM||||If the damage is really bad then my suggestion is replace the rear clip. You will save yourself a big headache. It also might be cheaper and I know faster to rep;ace the clip then to try to repair one. Again that depends on you and how bad is the damage. Me I would replace but that's just me. Enough said for my $0.02.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||04-13-2000||01:40 PM||||I had the same idea about changing the whole clip. I have a couple of questions though. 1st: How hard is it to remove? I know its all one piece up and over to the other side. 2nd: Do i have to reseal the rear window if i remove it? And just basicly how much of a job is it? All replies welcome and wanted..||||reg||5
Z||000005||jhar1987||04-13-2000||11:31 PM||||lenny is the body damaged around the deck lid? if so i just replaced the whole rear cowl on one of my fiero's. if this is what you need to replace it's fairly simple. I pulled one at a junk yard myself in about 2 hours.||||reg||1
